      "id": "sol.ahsme-1954-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The polynomial factors as \\[ \\begin{gathered} x^3+6x^2+11x+6\\\\ =(x+1)(x+2)(x+3). \\end{gathered} \\] Its roots are \\(-1,-2,-3,\\) so it has no positive real roots.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
